title: Field catalog and schema priority
tags: Schema
kind: reference
audience: dev
summary: The field catalogue lists what the schema declares as well as what the data has, and the schema's type wins a disagreement.

`GET /repos/:repo/fields` — the distinct field names with their value types — merges
the fields the data actually has with the ones the schema ''declares'' (every
constraint with a `type`). A field the schema declares and no metarecord carries yet
is listed; and where old data disagrees with the schema, the ''schema's type wins''
— consistent with delta validation: the data is never rewritten, the mismatch is a
violation `mf schema check` reports (`kind: type`).

That priority is silent in the catalogue itself. Clients surface the disagreements
separately and without blocking: the GUI runs a ''capped'' check once, when a
repository is opened, rather than listing every inconsistency — unusable on a large
repository.
